apiworkbench (1.3.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Hover help on every field, tab, button and badge: a card with a
    title, a plain explanation and an example. Can be turned off in
    Settings.
  * Layout fixes at phone, tablet and desktop sizes, larger touch
    targets on phones, and smoother theme switching.

 -- Dhivakar R <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:30:00 +0530

apiworkbench (1.2.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Postman import: collections (v1, v2.0, v2.1), single requests and
    folders, environments, globals and data exports, into a new or an
    existing collection or folder. Folders, auth inheritance, variables,
    every body type and common test-script checks carry over.
  * Folders in collections, collection variables, Postman dynamic
    variables, response captures, multipart form-data and binary bodies.
  * Redesigned interface: icon rail navigation, folder tree, breadcrumbs,
    Teal light/dark and Graphite themes, and a new logo.

 -- Dhivakar R <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 22:30:00 +0530

apiworkbench (1.1.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Load testing: run one request or a collection with up to 1,000
    parallel users, by iterations, duration or until stopped, with live
    throughput and latency percentiles. Every call can be logged with
    its response and saved as an HTML, CSV or JSON report.
  * Lower memory use: bounded runner history and response previews,
    cached JSON rendering, network clients closed when replaced.
  * Phone layout improvements.

 -- Dhivakar R <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Tue, 06 Oct 2026 02:30:00 +0530

apiworkbench (1.0.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix broken 1.0.0 package: the Flutter engine libraries
    (libflutter_linux_gtk.so, libapp.so) were stripped from the source
    tarball by dpkg-source's default ignore rules, so the app failed to
    launch. Override the ignore list via debian/source/options so the
    bundled libraries ship in the package.

 -- Dhivakar R <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Tue, 21 Jul 2026 03:15:00 +0530
